id: quiz.rust.channels
kind: quiz
track: rust
title: Choosing a channel type
question: Which channel do you use for a job queue, for fan-out, for the latest config value, and for a reply?
expects:
  - mpsc
  - broadcast
  - watch
  - oneshot
  - ownership
misuse:
  - unbounded mpsc for work => a slow consumer becomes an OOM
  - broadcast as a work queue => jobs are lost when a subscriber lags
related:
  - rust.tokio-mpsc
  - rust.tokio-broadcast
  - rust.tokio-watch
  - rust.tokio-oneshot
follow_ups:
  - what does a receiver see when all senders drop?
answer: |
  Bounded mpsc for a work queue (send().await is the backpressure); broadcast
  for fan-out where Lagged is handled by resyncing; watch for the latest value
  only; oneshot for a single reply. Sender drop closes the channel, which is the
  drain-and-exit signal.
